  {
   "id": "taxsim-co-refundable-credit-vintage",
   "concept": "us:tax/state-income-tax#liability",
   "kind": "amount_difference",
   "disposition": "upstream_engine_gap",
   "mechanism": "Triangulated TAXSIM-side divergence in Colorado's refundable credit\nstack (mirror of taxsim-co-refundable-credit-vintage in the\nintersection suite): on every selected row axiom and PolicyEngine\nagree on Colorado liability to the cent (the tax unit is absent from\nthe complete 31-row axiom-vs-PE mismatch set over the same 1,201-unit\npopulation), while TAXSIM departs. idtl=2 decomposition on the shared\ntax units locates the divergence in TAXSIM's state credit columns\n(sctc family-affordability/CTC, srebate) - its 2026-05-21 Colorado\nmodule carries a different family-affordability-credit vintage and\ncouples its Colorado EITC to its broken 2026 federal credit\nmachinery. Deltas are heterogeneous because the credit stack varies\nper household; the per-row proof is the axiom==PE agreement.",
